      "widgets_values": [
        "For the target video, at 0.00 seconds into the target video, <Picture 1> (from [Shot 1]) is fully referenced.\nintegrated_multimodal_description:\nPhotorealistic live-action cinematic style. Start exactly from the composition of <Picture 1>. Preserve the character identity, clothing, flower shop layout, vase position, and lighting direction. The video is exactly 5 seconds long and uses one continuous stable shot.\n[Shot 1]\n[0s-1.0s] The woman remains still, looking down at the white lisianthus in her right hand. Leaves outside the glass window move gently in the breeze.\n[1.0s-2.2s] She brings the flower close to her nose, gives a natural restrained smile, and says to the off-screen florist: <d>English Did these white lisianthus flowers arrive today?</d>\n[2.2s-3.3s] The off-screen florist replies warmly: <d>English They just arrived, still carrying the morning dew.</d> The woman looks up gently while maintaining a natural grip on the stem.\n[3.3s-4.5s] She places the white lisianthus into the glass vase beside the pale pink tulips. The flowers sway naturally and the water shows a subtle ripple.\n[4.5s-5.0s] She looks toward the off-screen person, gives a small nod, and holds a gentle smile. The camera makes one very slow, low-amplitude lateral movement while keeping the flower shop stable.\nCamera and transitions: One continuous medium shot. Begin almost static, then make one very subtle and slow lateral camera movement to reveal the woman, flowers, and bright window light. No cuts, dissolves, sudden zooms, handheld shake, duplicated people, extra people, duplicated flowers, or deformed hands.\nConstraints: Only one visible woman, white lisianthus, pale pink tulips, one glass vase, and the flower shop environment. No subtitles, logos, watermarks, readable text, extra fingers, floating flowers, clothing changes, or identity changes.\noverall_soundscape:\nA bright and quiet flower shop ambience with distant street noise, a soft breeze outside the window, a small sound of stems touching the glass vase, and a subtle ripple in the water. The dialogue must remain clear and synchronized with the actions.\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A.",
